[TITLE]
InpWriter round-trip fixture: dangling name references
Exercises defects 6, 7 and 8 in the only state that reaches them: the referenced
object does not exist, so the resolved index stays -1 while the parser's retained
name is all the writer has. A strict open rejects this model; the GUI opens for
editing with swmm_engine_set_lenient_open, which is exactly how a model in this
state reaches Save. Writing the index alone emitted '*' for the gage (fatal
ERROR 209 on reload) and the pump curve (a silent downgrade to IDEAL), and
dropped the snowpack column entirely.

[OPTIONS]
FLOW_UNITS           CFS
INFILTRATION         HORTON
FLOW_ROUTING         DYNWAVE
START_DATE           01/01/2020
START_TIME           00:00:00
END_DATE             01/02/2020
END_TIME             00:00:00
REPORT_STEP          00:15:00
WET_STEP             00:05:00
DRY_STEP             01:00:00
ROUTING_STEP         0:00:30
MIN_SLOPE            0

[EVAPORATION]
CONSTANT   0.0
DRY_ONLY   NO

[SUBCATCHMENTS]
;; RGX and SPX are never defined: gage / snowpack indices stay -1.
;;Name  RainGage  Outlet  Area  %Imperv  Width  %Slope  CurbLen  Snowpack
S1      RGX       J1      2.0   25.0     400.0  1.0     0        SPX

[SUBAREAS]
;;Subcatch  N-Imperv  N-Perv  S-Imperv  S-Perv  %ZeroImp  RouteTo
S1          0.01      0.10    0.05      0.05    25        OUTLET

[INFILTRATION]
;;Subcatch  MaxRate  MinRate  Decay  DryTime  MaxInfil
S1          3.0      0.5      4.0    7        0

[JUNCTIONS]
;;Name  Elev  MaxDepth  InitDepth  SurDepth  Aponded
J1       10.0  5.0       0          0         0
J2       9.0   5.0       0          0         0

[OUTFALLS]
;;Name  Elev  Type  StageData  Gated
O1       8.0   FREE  *          NO

[STORAGE]
;;Name  Elev  MaxDepth  InitDepth  Shape       Curve/Params
ST1      9.5   10.0      0          FUNCTIONAL  1000  0  0

[CONDUITS]
;;Name  FromNode  ToNode  Length  Roughness  InOffset  OutOffset
C1       J1        ST1     400.0   0.013      0         0
C2       J2        O1      400.0   0.013      0         0

[PUMPS]
;; PCX is never defined: the curve index stays -1. '*' here is the legal IDEAL
;; placeholder, so writing it loses the assignment without any diagnostic.
;;Name  FromNode  ToNode  PumpCurve  Status  Startup  Shutoff
P1       ST1       J2      PCX        ON      0        0

[XSECTIONS]
;;Link  Shape     Geom1  Geom2  Geom3  Geom4  Barrels
C1       CIRCULAR  1.5    0      0      0      1
C2       CIRCULAR  1.5    0      0      0      1

[REPORT]
INPUT       NO
CONTROLS    NO
SUBCATCHMENTS ALL
NODES       ALL
LINKS       ALL

[COORDINATES]
;;Node  X-Coord  Y-Coord
J1       0.0      0.0
J2       500.0    0.0
ST1      0.0      500.0
O1       1000.0   0.0
